<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> denote the latent payload communicated between colluding agents and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> the transcript features observed by the auditor. For each audited run <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math> we compute a bounded estimator <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}_{j}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}_{j}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> of the mutual information between <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>; the overall test statistic is the average <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\hat{I}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\hat{I}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Calibration produces a threshold <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> such that under the null hypothesis <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}:I(Z;X)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}:I(Z;X)=0</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\hat{I}&gt;\tau_{\alpha}]\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\hat{I}&gt;\tau_{\alpha}]\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Auditor interventions are modelled as stochastic maps <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> applied to the colluders’ channel. Data processing guarantees <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Z;\mathcal{T}(X))\leq I(Z;X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Z;\mathcal{T}(X))\leq I(Z;X)</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the capacity penalty</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=I(Z;X)-I(Z;\mathcal{T}(X))\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=I(Z;X)-I(Z;\mathcal{T}(X))\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which we estimate empirically via paired runs and report alongside surrogate diagnostics such as <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p_{X}\|p_{\mathcal{T}(X)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p_{X}\|p_{\mathcal{T}(X)})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Theorem 1</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Effective rate under interventions.</span> Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=I(Z;X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=I(Z;X)</annotation></semantics></math> be the payload rate achieved by the colluding strategy in the absence of interventions, and let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=I(Z;X)-I(Z;\mathcal{T}(X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=I(Z;X)-I(Z;\mathcal{T}(X))</annotation></semantics></math>. The preceding definition implies</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}_{j}]=I(Z;\mathcal{T}(X))=R-d" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}_{j}]=I(Z;\mathcal{T}(X))=R-d</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for each run <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>; the interventions reduce but do not eliminate the adversary’s channel capacity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Concentration of the empirical statistic.</span> The variables <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}_{1},\dots,\hat{I}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}_{1},\dots,\hat{I}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent and bounded in <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Hoeffding’s inequality states that for any <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\big[\hat{I}-\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]\leq-t\big]\leq\exp(-2mt^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\big[\hat{I}-\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]\leq-t\big]\leq\exp(-2mt^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Setting <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]-\tau_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]-\tau_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\big[\hat{I}\leq\tau_{\alpha}\big]\leq\exp\Big(-2m\big(\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]-\tau_{\alpha}\big)^{2}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\big[\hat{I}\leq\tau_{\alpha}\big]\leq\exp\Big(-2m\big(\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]-\tau_{\alpha}\big)^{2}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Combining the bounds.</span> Under the alternative hypothesis we have <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]\geq R-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]\geq R-d</annotation></semantics></math>. Whenever <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;d+\tau_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;d+\tau_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]-\tau_{\alpha}\geq R-d-\tau_{\alpha}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{I}]-\tau_{\alpha}\geq R-d-\tau_{\alpha}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\big[\hat{I}\leq\tau_{\alpha}\big]\leq\exp\left(-2m(R-d-\tau_{\alpha})^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\big[\hat{I}\leq\tau_{\alpha}\big]\leq\exp\left(-2m(R-d-\tau_{\alpha})^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The type-II error of the MI detector is thus bounded by the right-hand side, and the true positive rate obeys</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TPR}\geq 1-\exp\left(-2m(R-d-\tau_{\alpha})^{2}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TPR</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TPR}\geq 1-\exp\left(-2m(R-d-\tau_{\alpha})^{2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">which is the statement of Theorem 1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Detector Threshold Tables</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Comprehensive per-detector thresholds (mean, standard deviation, p95, p99, target FPR levels) are recorded in <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">results/calibration/detector_thresholds.json</span> and visualised in <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">notebooks/detector_calibration.ipynb</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Additional Figures</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reproducible notebooks generate MI versus reward trade-off plots, fairness gap distributions, and intervention hit-rate histograms. All figures can be regenerated via <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">scripts/regenerate_results.py</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Residual Risks</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">docs/residual_risks.md</span> enumerates open challenges including fairness metadata dependencies, linguistic signal weakness, and sample-efficiency considerations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
